<section id="summary">
<h2>1 Executive Summary</h2>
<p>The units module is a quantity-conversion and calculation-history library. Analysis is performed to determine how its public interfaces support unit-aware calculations, and the key results are summarized below.</p>
<ul>
<li>Explicitly labelled quantities can be converted and multiplied while their operation history is preserved.
<ul><li>The public pressure–area example gives {{ display.force_kn }} kN for {{ display.pressure_kpa }} kPa acting uniformly over {{ display.area_m2 }} m². This is a surface-force magnitude; an allowable load and opposing pressure are not supplied, so capacity and net force are not evaluated.</li></ul></li>
<li>The module can support the numerical part of a calculation record.
<ul><li>The source label and operation history do not establish measurement quality or physical validity. Raw numeric inputs at decorated interfaces bypass unit conversion, as described in <a href="#limits">Section 7</a>.</li></ul></li>
</ul>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Revision</th><th>Date</th><th>Change and reason</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A</td><td>22 October 2026</td><td>First issue: public conversion and force examples are described to distinguish calculation output from engineering acceptance.</td></tr></tbody><caption>Revision history. The initial issue establishes the module description and its limits.</caption></table></div>
</section>
<section id="introduction">
<h2>2 Introduction</h2>
<p>The scope and intended use of the quantity workflow are described here. The module is used to attach units to magnitudes, convert compatible quantities and record arithmetic history.</p>
<p>The main workflow covers explicit input quantities, dimensional checking, conversion, multiplication and an audit export. Its public entry points are documented in the repository guide, identified in <a href="#repository-records">Section 9.2</a>. The result can be passed to a separate engineering assessment once the physical basis and acceptance criterion are supplied.</p>
<h3>2.1 Not covered</h3>
<p>The additional sub-areas are identified without extending the worked-example conclusion to them. Commodity-energy adapters, environmental-data adapters, offshore field mappings, automatic input inference, display templates, policy enforcement and lineage rendering are not evaluated as engineering models in this report.</p>
<p>Their interfaces and existing tests are listed in <a href="#repository-records">Section 9.2</a>. External integrations are outside the assessed workflow.</p>
</section>
