<section id="symbols">
<h2>10 Acronyms and Symbols</h2>
<p>The quantities and abbreviations used in the report are defined here. Their units refer to the selected pressure–area example.</p>
<p><var>F</var> denotes normal surface force in newtons or kilonewtons; <var>p</var> denotes uniform pressure in pascals or kilopascals; <var>A</var> denotes loaded area in square metres. <var>x</var> denotes numerical magnitude and <var>c</var> denotes a multiplicative unit scale relative to a common reference.</p>
<p>SI denotes the International System of Units. NIST denotes the National Institute of Standards and Technology. Pa, kPa, N, kN, m and mm denote pascal, kilopascal, newton, kilonewton, metre and millimetre. JSON denotes JavaScript Object Notation; CSV denotes comma-separated values. SHA-256 denotes the content-digest algorithm used in the source record. NOT_EVALUATED means that the required basis is absent; ASSUMED - to be confirmed identifies an idealization requiring physical confirmation.</p>
</section>
