<p>Input inference only traverses a flat dictionary and recognizes exact field names; it does not read a configuration file. Explicit units take precedence, unknown fields remain unchanged, and array inputs are outside the scalar inference path. The offshore field dictionary does not automatically extend that parser.</p>
<p>The policy implementation only rejects a mismatched known quantity when strict mode is enabled and automatic conversion is disabled. Both switches need to be specified for rejection. An unknown quantity type passes through. The formatter's direct precision argument is superseded by its resolved template; an explicit template is the documented control.</p>
<p>Energy adapters use literal mapping keys and can reject dimensionally incompatible pairs. Some gas-labelled registry aliases are defined as energy equivalents rather than physical gas volumes. Published commodity-factor metadata is absent in the inspected registry; numerical commodity coefficients are excluded from this report.</p>
<p>Array and offset-temperature behaviour, cross-registry operations, input finiteness, uncertainty propagation, tamper evidence and dependency-graph accuracy are outside the numerical example. Domain adapters return plain magnitudes; the missing-value path in the environmental adapter returns no quantity. These interfaces require their own application-specific input checks.</p>
</section>
<section id="appendix-b">
<h2>Appendix B Validation and Quality Evidence</h2>
<p>The repository evidence and the new numerical checks are distinguished here. Software checks establish the behaviours they assert; field agreement and a complete engineering qualification are not established.</p>
<p>The existing registry and quantity tests assert compatible conversions, arithmetic and incompatible addition. The integration tests exercise configuration parsing, unit policy, round trips, audit serialization, formatting and lineage construction. A round trip is a consistency check; reciprocal conversion errors can cancel. No saved measured benchmark dataset for the selected pressure–area example is identified in these records.</p>
<p>The report adds hand-calculated pressure, force and length anchors using the external theory in Section 4. The arithmetic is written above each assertion. Separate consistency checks compare every worked-example value and curve point with a fresh module call, and the displayed inputs are multiplied to recover the headline result.</p>
<p>The rebuild check compares rounded payload values with tolerance and compares the remaining document text with the committed copy. Calculation-source digest differences identify stale evidence and name the rebuild command. UTF-8 and line-feed output are checked, and the report tests are exercised with the Python UTF-8 override unset.</p>
<p>The delivery checks cover section structure, local pointers, standalone assets, public wording and the comment-save logic. Browser-rendered layout, measured operating data and licensed integration behaviour are not evaluated by these checks.</p>
<p>Quality pre-flight evidence is held by the report tests in Section 9.2: the inputs have public source locations, the equations have external references, missing physical criteria remain explicit, the summary preserves the surface-force qualifier, and numerical outputs are rebuilt from module calls. Reviewer comments are exported as a separate local JSON file; they are not sent to a service.</p>
</section>
